# Requests to drive the demo from VS Code (REST Client) or Rider/Visual Studio.
# Start the AppHost first: `dotnet run --project apphost`.
@orders = http://localhost:5300
@shipping = http://localhost:5310
@dispatcher = http://localhost:5320

### 1. Place an order the outbox way: order + outbox row in one transaction (202 Accepted)
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "Ada", "product": "Keyboard", "quantity": 1 }

### 2. Look at the outbox: the relay moves the row from pending to sent within ~1 second
GET {{orders}}/api/outbox

### 3. The dispatcher called Shipping, which created the shipment and stored the idempotency key
GET {{shipping}}/api/shipments

###
GET {{shipping}}/api/inbox

### 4. Replay a message (paste an outbox id): it's sent again and Shipping ignores the duplicate
POST {{orders}}/api/outbox/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/replay

### 4b. Dispatcher crash: Shipping does the work, then the dispatcher "dies" before completing the
###     message. Turn it on, place an order (request 1) and check the deliveries: delivery 1 is
###     "simulated-crash", delivery 2 is "already-processed", and there is still ONE shipment.
PUT {{dispatcher}}/api/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "crashAfterDelivery": true }

###
GET {{dispatcher}}/api/deliveries

###
PUT {{dispatcher}}/api/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "crashAfterDelivery": false }

### 5. The naive way: commit, then call Shipping over HTTP. Stop "shipping" in the Aspire
###    dashboard first, and the order is saved but no shipment will ever exist.
POST {{orders}}/api/orders/naive
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "Grace", "product": "Mouse", "quantity": 2 }

### 6. Chaos on: Shipping answers 503, the dispatcher abandons, Service Bus retries 5 times, then dead-letters
PUT {{shipping}}/api/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failProcessing": true }

### 7. Dead-letter queue (peek)
GET {{dispatcher}}/api/dead-letters

### 8. Chaos off, then resubmit the dead letters
PUT {{shipping}}/api/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "failProcessing": false }

###
POST {{dispatcher}}/api/dead-letters/resubmit
